00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.280
KEIJI KANAZAWA:
Today, unlocking AI

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.770
for your business needs
means asking a few

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.090
important questions.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.740
How can it help you grow?

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.520
How can it help increase
customer satisfaction?

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.660
How can AI accelerate and
optimize your workflows?

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.260
The answer increasingly
comes from applications

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:01.620
and agents built on top of an AI
platform like Microsoft Foundry.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.430
That's because enterprises,
startups need the right models,

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:09.360
agents, and tools to build
enterprise-ready AI agents

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.410
and apps.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.280
You need to be able

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.000
to orchestrate multiple
agents together with support

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.600
for interoperability
and open frameworks.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.000
You need access to
the best models

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.430
like Claude for your use case.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.490
And then you need to
connect the agents

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.010
to different knowledge
sources and tools

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:34.680
like your enterprise data, like
Microsoft 365 or your databases.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.240
Once you've built those agents,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.570
you need to continuously
monitor, observe,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.840
and evaluate your solutions
through every stage

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.710
of the AI development lifecycle
with proper content safety,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:51.300
observability, and evaluation
tools in every layer

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.690
of your AI apps and agents.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:59.310
And AI agents should be
able to tune, customize,

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.120
and improve over time
continuously using things

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.390
like optimizing your
skills and prompts,

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.310
as well as fine-tuning models
when that's available.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.060
And last but not least, you need
to deploy your apps to the local

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.980
and to the edge in order for you
or your customers to be able

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.410
to take advantage of the agents.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.340
Now, agentic applications
are not just

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.420
about calling a model once
and getting a response back.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.910
Agentic applications
increasingly involve

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.270
long-running systems
that reason and act

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:44.190
and then continuously learn
from context and execution.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.860
These are goal-driven processes

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.610
where agents automatically
execute tasks

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:54.810
and optimize the outcomes
towards general goal rubrics

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.540
that describe the
desired outcomes.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:02.190
For example, let's say I'm
observing a spike in traffic

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.860
or a dip in success rates.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.430
Before agents, you might go
look at dashboards yourself,

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.560
write and run
queries, use Excel,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.750
come up with some hypotheses.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.740
With agents, once I set it
up with the right models,

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.070
the right contacts, things
like lifecycle metrics,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:25.260
support tickets, CRM
databases, and email messages,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.390
they can take a question.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.070
What's causing the spike?

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:32.010
And the agent will create
a plan, execute it,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.400
and loop until it has some
answers and generate,

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.370
for example, a nice HTML
report for you instead

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.900
of you having to do it.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.100
So that involves coordinating
models and tools,

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:48.120
being able to reason through
complex, long-running processes,

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.410
coordinating multiple models
with different capabilities,

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.650
like maybe there's a good
model that's really skilled

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.840
at parsing PDFs.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.570
We all work with PDFs daily.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:04.290
Turns out PDF is still
not a small problem.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.470
So you might need to do
special handling depending

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.890
on your domain for how you
process those documents.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.700
And so the power really comes
from giving the agent access

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:21.030
to your deep business context,
things like Microsoft 365 Graph,

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.280
enterprise data in
Azure, and other systems

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.840
across your organization.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.860
Increasingly, agentic
applications also use concepts

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.700
like memory and
involve self-learning

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:37.590
and self-improving loops, where
based on observing the outcomes

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.680
of the agents, you can
improve the skills,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.420
you can improve the workflows,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.090
so that they stay
relevant over time.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:51.330
And so that comes with
the agent AI lifecycle,

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:55.740
which involves building
the agent, deploying it,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:00.270
operating it, all in a
secure governed framework,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:04.580
suited for enterprises,
and requires evaluating

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.730
and monitoring your
agents over time.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:12.360
As you observe the agent's
operation, you need to be able

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.970
to mitigate if there
are any issues,

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:18.510
and then optimize
the agent over time.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.010
So it's not a one-shot thing

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.530
where you just deploy
the agent once.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.690
You need to continually iterate.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.080
You need to continually
evolve with your customers,

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.380
with the data, and with
the marketplace in order

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:36.340
to get the most effective use of
the AI agents for your domain.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.460
And this is why Microsoft
