00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:55.340
Now let's get into
a little bit deeper

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.950
into what an agent
actually does.

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:01.370
An agent is built
using frontier models

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:06.240
like the Claude series inside
what you may have heard called

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.290
a harness.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:08.940
We'll come back to
that a little bit.

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:12.900
A harness drives model
inference and allows the model

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:18.300
to write code, invoke tools,
receive inputs, process them,

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:20.220
and iterate in a loop.

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:23.100
This is often called
the agentic loop.

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:26.070
The agent takes the input,
reasons about what needs

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:30.120
to happen, calls tools or
retrieves information,

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:34.380
and then continues until it can
produce what it considers the

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.070
right output.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:39.960
Foundry Agent
Service is the part

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:43.530
of Microsoft Foundry that's
designed to be the best place

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:49.080
to build and run AI apps
and agents that scale.

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.880
It's open by design.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:53.850
You can work with different
frameworks and protocols,

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:57.780
including the agent-to-agent
protocol, MCP,

00:20:57.780 --> 00:20:59.880
and other emerging standards.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.760
It's built for
multi-agent workflows

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:06.840
and supports the agent
framework of your choice.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:10.650
With Foundry agent service, you
can access models in Foundry,

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:15.510
connect to Foundry IQ, and other
data sources, leverage tools,

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:18.300
and deploy them in production

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:22.710
in a secure enterprise-grade
platform that you can observe,

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:26.970
monitor, and optimize
and improve over time.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:30.390
You can deploy your agents,
not just within Foundry,

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:36.610
but also to Microsoft
365 and Agent 365.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:40.650
And you get that
end-to-end observability

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:45.450
and simplified governance
that's underpinning everything

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.710
in Microsoft Foundry.

